# Copy to deploy/deploy.env in each checkout on the VPS. Not committed —
# it is what tells one checkout apart from the other.
#
# The live site, in ~/FarmHand:
#
#   SITE=prod
#   BRANCH=main
#   WEB_ROOT=/var/www/farmhand
#
# The dev site, in ~/FarmHand-dev:
#
#   SITE=dev
#   BRANCH=dev
#   WEB_ROOT=/var/www/farmhand-dev
#   PROD_REPO=/home/YOU/FarmHand
#
# SITE also reaches the build (as VITE_SITE_ENV), which is what puts the
# "dev build" banner on the dev site and leaves the live one unmarked.
#
# BRANCH is checked before anything is built: deploy.sh refuses to run if
# the checkout is on a different branch, so running it in the wrong
# directory fails loudly instead of publishing dev's code to the live site.
#
# PROD_REPO is only read by promote.sh, from the dev checkout — it is the
# live site's checkout, the one it deploys after pushing to main.

SITE=prod
BRANCH=main
WEB_ROOT=/var/www/farmhand
